  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["T7", "T6", "T8", "T2"],
      "pins": ["T7.3", "T6.1", "T8.1", "T2.3"],
      "nets": ["/NET0059", "/NET0089"],
      "observed": "The main-pump MOSFET T6 (IRLR2905) gate net /NET0089 contains only the 100 Ω drive resistor R21 from ESP32 IO10 and the 10 kΩ pull-up R16; it has no BT3904 collector connected to it. The second BT3904, T7, whose base is driven from the FLOAT_LOW signal IO0 through R48, has its collector tied to /NET0059, the ATO-valve gate net, together with T2 and T8.",
      "expected": "The specification states that the main circulation pump MOSFET is gate-driven through a 100 Ω resistor and pre-driven by a BT3904 NPN level shifter, and that float switches provide low-level pump cutoff interlocks. The low-level float path should therefore be connected to the main-pump gate net (/NET0089) through a BT3904 collector, not to the ATO-valve gate net.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"61\") (name \"/NET0089\") (node (ref \"R16\") (pin \"1\")) (node (ref \"R21\") (pin \"2\")) (node (ref \"T6\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"G\") (pintype \"passive\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"41\") (name \"/NET0059\") (node (ref \"R44\") (pin \"2\")) (node (ref \"R53\") (pin \"2\")) (node (ref \"T2\") (pin \"3\") (pinfunction \"C\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"T7\") (pin \"3\") (pinfunction \"C\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"T8\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"G\") (pintype \"passive\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "T2 — IRLR2905 ... gate driven through R1 (100 Ω) from the ESP32 pin, pre-driven via T1 (BT3904 NPN level shifter)."
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "float-switch interlocks for low-level pump cutoff and high-level overflow protection"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The intended hardware low-level pump cutoff interlock is missing: the main pump can remain enabled by GPIO10 even when the low-level float condition is asserted, while the low-level float instead disables the ATO valve. This can allow dry-running of the circulation pump and changes the intended safety interlock behavior.",
      "confidence": 0.66
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The connectivity shows the main pump gate net lacks the BT3904 predriver/interlock described in the specification; the low-level float transistor T7 is tied to the ATO-valve gate net instead of the pump gate net, which is a deviation from the intended float-switch pump-cutoff interlock."
}

